<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  operator.sdf - camera-visible yellow operator body for the SafeCollab cell.

  PURPOSE
  The overhead camera in cell.xacro feeds perception_node, which runs an HSV
  colour-blob detector (detect_human(), hue_low=20..hue_high=40, OpenCV 0-180
  scale).  Yellow RGB (1.0, 1.0, 0.0) maps to HSV hue ~30 (OpenCV), squarely
  inside that window, so the camera detects this body wherever it appears in
  the frame.

  MODEL PROPERTIES
  Static (no physics). A FLAT 0.35 x 0.35 x 0.08 m yellow puck — deliberately
  thin. The overhead camera recovers the operator's planar position by
  back-projecting the blob centroid onto a single plane (perception_node
  plane_z_m == human_node._MARKER_Z == 0.95 m). A tall box, viewed at the
  camera's ~21 deg off-vertical angle, projects a silhouette whose centroid is
  biased outward (its top face is farther from the camera nadir), corrupting
  the recovered (x, y). A flat puck centred on the plane has almost no such
  bias, so the perceived pose tracks the operator across the whole path. The
  0.35 x 0.35 footprint keeps the blob well above min_area_px=100 at the wider
  (hfov=1.5) camera. No collision geometry: purely a visual marker.

  POSE TRACKING
  cell.launch.py spawns this model at the path start-position
  (x=0.9, y=0.0, z=0.95).  human_node calls the gz transport service
  /world/empty/set_pose at 10 Hz to move it in X/Y with the operator while
  holding z at the constant marker height (_MARKER_Z).  The full 3-D
  world-&gt;human_gt TF (incl. the reaching hand's z) is broadcast at 50 Hz
  independently.
-->
<sdf version="1.8">
  <model name="operator">
    <static>true</static>
    <link name="body">
      <visual name="visual">
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.35 0.35 0.08</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <!--
            Yellow: R=1.0 G=1.0 B=0.0 (linear sRGB).
            OpenCV HSV (H in [0,180]): hue = 30.
            perception_node.detect_human() window: hue_low=20, hue_high=40.
            sat_low=100, val_low=100 - bright saturated yellow satisfies both.
            emissive term ensures the body stays visible under dim gz lighting.
          -->
          <ambient>1.0 1.0 0.0 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>1.0 1.0 0.0 1.0</diffuse>
          <specular>0.1 0.1 0.0 1.0</specular>
          <emissive>0.1 0.1 0.0 1.0</emissive>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>
  </model>
</sdf>
